---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Your drawings. Your computer."
  description="How the ENG Drawing Viewer website and desktop application handle your information."
>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <div class="section-tag">PRIVACY</div>
      <h1>
        Your drawings.
        <br />
        <span>Your computer.</span>
      </h1>
      <p>
        Privacy should be straightforward. Here is what happens on this website
        and in the desktop workspace.
      </p>
    </header>
    <article class="page-content prose">
      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        The website has no analytics, advertising, accounts, tracking cookies or
        document upload service. Fonts, scripts, styles and product images are
        served with the site. Interactive demonstrations run in your browser and
        do not transmit their contents.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you choose a colour theme, your browser stores that preference
        locally under <code>eng-theme</code>. Clear the site’s local storage to
        remove it. The MARK web demonstration lives only in the current tab.
      </p>
      <h2>GitHub hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is intended for GitHub Pages hosting. GitHub may process
        technical connection information, including IP addresses, to operate its
        service. Downloads, when available, are hosted on GitHub Releases.
        GitHub’s handling of that information is described in its{' '}
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">
          privacy statement
        </a>
        .
      </p>
      <h2>The desktop application</h2>
      <p>
        Viewing, markup, conversion and PowerPoint generation run locally. The
        application has no user account, telemetry or cloud processing workflow.
        Original drawing files are opened without modifying them. Exports are
        saved as new files you choose.
      </p>
      <p>
        Local settings include your theme, recent folders and export
        preferences. A thumbnail cache speeds up browsing. Diagnostic logs can
        contain local paths and filenames. Review logs before attaching them to
        a public issue.
      </p>
      <p>
        On macOS these files are stored in the standard Application Support,
        Caches and Logs folders under <code>ENG Drawing Viewer</code> in your
        user Library. Scans default to{' '}
        <code>~/Documents/ENG Drawing Viewer Scans</code>. The thumbnail cache
        can be cleared in Settings; removing the app alone does not delete these
        folders.
      </p>
      <h2>Optional local tools</h2>
      <p>
        Office-to-PDF conversion needs LibreOffice installed locally. Scan with
        iPhone uses Apple Continuity Camera and nearby Apple devices; Apple’s
        operating system services have their own privacy settings. Choosing that
        feature initiates the device interaction.
      </p>
      <h2>Support</h2>
      <p>
        GitHub Issues are public. Use fictional sample drawings, remove
        confidential details, and inspect screenshots and logs before posting.
        Never post credentials or private engineering documents.
      </p>
      <p>Last updated: 24 October 2026.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
